<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Arranging letters of words with repeated letters</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the number of distinct arrangements of the letters in each word. Recall that when some items are identical, we divide the total arrangements \(n!\) by the factorial of each repeated group:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Number of arrangements} = \frac{n!}{r_1! \times r_2! \times \cdots}\)</p>

<p><b>Part A: Arrange all the letters of the word {@word_a@}.</b></p>
<ol>
  <li>Total number of letters in <b>{@word_a@}</b>:<br>
  \(n =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]
  </li>
  <li>Count the repeated letters ({@sing_a@}):<br>
  The letter <b>{@let_a1@}</b> appears [[input:ans2]] times and the letter <b>{@let_a2@}</b> appears [[input:ans3]] times.
  <div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
  <div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
  </li>
  <li>Evaluate the number of distinct arrangements \(\displaystyle \frac{{@n_a@}!}{{@r_a1@}! \times {@r_a2@}!}\):<br>
  \(\displaystyle \text{Number of arrangements} = \frac{{@n_a@}!}{{@r_a1@}! \times {@r_a2@}!} =\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]
  </li>
</ol>

<p><b>Part B: Arrange all the letters of the word {@word_b@}.</b></p>
<ol>
  <li>Total number of letters in <b>{@word_b@}</b>:<br>
  \(n =\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt5]]
  </li>
  <li>Count the repeated letters ({@sing_b@}):<br>
  The letter <b>{@let_b1@}</b> appears [[input:ans6]] times, the letter <b>{@let_b2@}</b> appears [[input:ans7]] times, and the letter <b>{@let_b3@}</b> appears [[input:ans8]] times.
  <div>[[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt6]]</div>
  <div>[[validation:ans7]] [[feedback:prt7]]</div>
  <div>[[validation:ans8]] [[feedback:prt8]]</div>
  </li>
  <li>Evaluate the number of distinct arrangements \(\displaystyle \frac{{@n_b@}!}{{@r_b1@}! \times {@r_b2@}! \times {@r_b3@}!}\):<br>
  \(\displaystyle \text{Number of arrangements} = \frac{{@n_b@}!}{{@r_b1@}! \times {@r_b2@}! \times {@r_b3@}!} =\) [[input:ans9]] [[validation:ans9]] [[feedback:prt9]]
  </li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>Count the total number of letters \(n\), then identify each repeated letter. Because swapping identical letters does not produce a new arrangement, divide \(n!\) by the factorial of each repeated group.</p>

<p><b>Part A: Word {@word_a@}</b><br>
There are \(n = {@n_a@}\) letters in total, with <b>{@let_a1@}</b> appearing \({@r_a1@}\) times and <b>{@let_a2@}</b> appearing \({@r_a2@}\) times ({@sing_a@}). Expand \({@n_a@}!\) until it matches the largest denominator factorial and cancel:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@n_a@}!}{{@r_a1@}! \times {@r_a2@}!} = {@steps_a@} = {@ta4@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Arrangements for {@word_a@}} = {@ta4@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part B: Word {@word_b@}</b><br>
There are \(n = {@n_b@}\) letters in total, with <b>{@let_b1@}</b> appearing \({@r_b1@}\) times, <b>{@let_b2@}</b> appearing \({@r_b2@}\) times, and <b>{@let_b3@}</b> appearing \({@r_b3@}\) times ({@sing_b@}). Expand \({@n_b@}!\) until it matches the largest denominator factorial and cancel:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \frac{{@n_b@}!}{{@r_b1@}! \times {@r_b2@}! \times {@r_b3@}!} = {@steps_b@} = {@ta9@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Arrangements for {@word_b@}} = {@ta9@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
